ient like SlskdClient(Protocol) in slskd.py:96. That is consistent with the existing transfer client, which never had one, so it is not a finding.","Existing response handling in _request_json covers the DELETE path: 204 or an empty body returns {}, and 401/403/429/5xx classification is shared. Semantics for 404 (transfer already gone) are not handled specially. A 404 raises TransferEnqueueError('unavailable'), which may be wrong for an idempotent cancel. That is a behavior/product question for the bugs lane, not an architecture finding."]}
